## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **Functional/D365/CodeFiles/WebResources/WebResources/scripts/ribbons/constructionNoticeRibbon.ts** (`createCmsEntry`): Only CMS-integration code in the entire repo (verified via CodeGraph explore + ripgrep for 'preview'/'cms'/'PSME'/'cmsentryurl': no live-preview, GO/UP-brand, or CMS-rendering code exists in this codebase — the CMS itself is the external PSME system reached via the 'mlx_GanericPluginForPSMEIntergration' action). This function is where the CMS entry URLs (mlx_imcmsentryurl / mlx_mxcmsentryurl — the links that open CMS content) are requested and computed, not merely displayed; the display/visibility logic lives in the BR-CNIMMXURLDisplayRules workflow XAML, which only reads those fields. The early-return guard means once URLs exist, no new CMS request (e.g. a preview/draft render) can ever be issued from the record, which is the causal blocker for a 'live preview of CMS content' capability on the C365 side.
  - **Minimal fix:** The minimal C365-side change is in createCmsEntry: the unconditional early return `if (imUrl || mxUrl) { return; }` prevents any further CMS operation once URLs exist, so a live-preview request can never be sent. Change the guard so it only skips the initial URL-generation case and still issues the `mlx_GanericPluginForPSMEIntergration` request (reusing the existing request/getMetadata block at lines 117-136) when a preview of current content is needed — i.e. pass a distinct OperationType (e.g. "Preview" alongside the existing literal "CMS" at line 120) instead of returning. Note: no existing helper for preview/draft rendering exists in this repo (ripgrep for 'preview' across source returned only unrelated dashboard/SavedQuery XML), and no GO/UP-brand CMS code exists here at all — if the ticket's acceptance criteria concern previewing content inside the CMS authoring UI itself, the fix belongs in the external PSME/CMS system, not this repository.


